  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1203 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nSouthwest flow aloft will be back on the upswing Thu/Fri ahead of\nan upper level low, forecast to fill and open up as it progresses\neast from the west coast through the Great Basin. Windy conditions\nare forecast Friday, especially across northeast NM due in part to\nanother deepening side trough. QPF continues to trend down across\nnorthern NM with this trough as it moves east across the southern\nRockies. However, lower snow levels and stronger westerly flow \nwill bring orographic forcing, allowing for some snow accumulation\nacross the northern mountains Friday night into Saturday morning,\nfavoring the Tusas Mountains. The weekend is looking uneventful \nat this time, but there is growing model agreement on a quick- \nhitting upper level trough/low bringing a more widespread round of\nprecipitation Mon/Tue of next week.",
